[{"id":4363150411,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOEFLz888AAAABBBBkSw","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Approach is right — backfills the data [#3197](https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3197) and [#3199](https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3199) explicitly left out. `WHERE expiry IS NOT NULL AND expiry < '1900-01-01'` is robust on both SQLite (lex compare, `'0' < '1'`) and Postgres (implicit timestamp cast). Test covers the five interesting expiry states.\n\nTwo small nits to fix before merge:\n\n1. Drop the `#3197` / `#3199` refs and the `Fixes:` URL from the source comment in `hscontrol/db/db.go`. Those belong in the commit message and `CHANGELOG.md`, not next to the SQL. The prose (\"versions before 0.28 persisted a pointer to a zero `time.Time`…\") stands on its own.\n\n2. Repo uses Go-style `package: imperative` for titles, not Conventional Commits — recent log has `db: scope DestroyUser …`, `state: fix policy change race …`. Suggest renaming to `db: backfill zero-time node expiry to NULL`.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pul